course: dictionary
lesson: 417
title: The word apprentice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An apprentice is a person who learns a job or skill by working alongside an expert. Think of it as learning by doing: the apprentice watches, helps and practises until they can do the work well.
explain: «For centuries most people learned jobs as apprentices, living and working with a master for years.» The clues are living and working with a master. The apprentice learns from someone skilled, and the learning goes on for a set time. Here, master means a skilled expert who teaches.
explain: The word can also be used more widely. A beginner who learns from an expert in any field, such as music or science, is an apprentice too. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "She is an apprentice pianist" makes sense, because she is learning from a skilled teacher.
fact: An apprentice is a young person who learns a trade or skill by working with a skilled worker.
fact: Apprentices usually work for a set time and receive a small wage.
fact: «Apprentice» can also mean any beginner learning from an expert.
fact: Apprentices train for jobs such as builders, mechanics, hairdressers and chefs.
fact: «Be apprenticed to» means to be sent to work and learn under a master.
exercise: What is an apprentice? | *A beginner who learns a skill by working with an expert | A tool that builders use to cut wood | A boss who hires workers for a day | A teacher who never stops giving lessons
exercise: Which job might an apprentice train for? | A rainbow | *A builder | The moon | A river
exercise: In «living and working with a master for years», what does master mean? | A ship that sails far away | A dog that barks loudly | A person who is always late | *A skilled expert who teaches
test: What does «be apprenticed to» mean? | To be sent home early from school | To be the boss of a shop | *To be sent to work and learn under a master
test: In «an apprentice electrician», which word tells you the person is still learning? | an | electrician | the | *apprentice
exam: Ben says an apprentice is a boss who gives orders to experts. What is the right meaning? | A tool for cutting wood | *A young person learning a trade from a skilled worker | A person who retires early | A boss who gives orders to experts
